# {{ site.name }}

> {{ site.tagline }}

Airfoils, Incorporated is an aerodynamic consulting firm founded and led by
Dan M. Somers, an internationally recognized expert in airfoil design,
analysis, and wind-tunnel testing. The firm is based in Port Matilda,
Pennsylvania, USA.

## About Dan M. Somers

Dan M. Somers holds a B.S. in Aeronautical Engineering from Purdue University
(1974). He served as a Research Engineer at NASA Langley Research Center from
1974 to 1989 and founded Airfoils, Incorporated in 1980. He co-developed the
Eppler Airfoil Design and Analysis Code with Richard Eppler and has designed
airfoils for wind turbines, aircraft, gyroplanes, sailplanes, unmanned aerial
vehicles, cruise missiles, and cooling-tower fans.

## Key Capabilities

- Custom airfoil design using the Eppler code (conformal-mapping design,
  panel-method analysis, integral boundary-layer methods)
- Experimental verification through wind-tunnel testing at world-class
  facilities (NASA Langley LTPT, Delft University, Penn State, DLR)
- Design of high-lift systems
- Applications spanning wind energy, general aviation, business jets, commuter
  aircraft, gyroplanes, UAVs, sailplanes, and industrial fans

## Major Clients

- National Renewable Energy Laboratory (NREL) — wind turbines
- Groen Brothers Aviation — gyroplanes
- Naval Air Warfare Center (NAWC) — unmanned aerial vehicles

